---
/** Scoring formats overview page. Ported from react/pages/Scoring.tsx. */
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import BackLink from "../../components/BackLink.astro";
---

<Base title="GlideComp - Scoring">
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-background text-foreground py-6 px-page-safe">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <header class="mb-10">
        <BackLink href="/" />
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold flex items-center gap-3">
          <img src="/icon.svg" alt="GlideComp logo" class="w-8 h-8" />
          Scoring
        </h1>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1">How GlideComp scores competitions</p>
      </header>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <div class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          <p class="text-muted-foreground">
            Every GlideComp competition uses one of two scoring formats. The organiser selects
            the format in the competition settings. Select a format below to read how it works.
            The last two pages describe the checks that GlideComp makes on each tracklog before
            it scores.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      {/* GAP */}
      <a
        href="/scoring/gap"
        class="block mb-6 p-5 rounded-lg border border-border bg-card hover:border-primary/60 transition-colors group"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">
            GAP <span class="text-sm font-normal text-muted-foreground">race to goal</span>
          </h2>
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="18"
            height="18"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            class="text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-foreground transition-colors"
          >
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
            <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          The standard CIVL scoring, used at most paragliding and hang gliding competitions.
          Pilots race a set course through turnpoints to a goal. A perfect task day is worth 1000
          points. GAP shares those points between distance, time, leading and arrival, by how
          each pilot performed against the field. Use GAP for a task with a defined route and
          goal.
        </p>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-medium mt-3 text-foreground group-hover:underline">
          Read how GAP works
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="14"
            height="14"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
            <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
          </svg>
        </span>
      </a>

      {/* Open Distance */}
      <a
        href="/scoring/open-distance"
        class="block mb-6 p-5 rounded-lg border border-border bg-card hover:border-primary/60 transition-colors group"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">
            Open distance
            <span class="text-sm font-normal text-muted-foreground">
              fly as far as you can
            </span>
          </h2>
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="18"
            height="18"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            class="text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-foreground transition-colors"
          >
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
            <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          All pilots launch from the same place and fly as far as they can. There is no set goal.
          Each task has one take-off turnpoint. Your score is the metres of open distance you
          flew. That is the straight-line distance from the point where you leave the take-off
          cylinder, to the furthest point you reached. Use open distance for free-distance and
          record-style days.
        </p>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-medium mt-3 text-foreground group-hover:underline">
          Read how open distance works
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="14"
            height="14"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
            <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
          </svg>
        </span>
      </a>

      {/* Data cleaning */}
      <a
        href="/scoring/data-cleaning"
        class="block mb-6 p-5 rounded-lg border border-border bg-card hover:border-primary/60 transition-colors group"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">
            Track data cleaning
            <span class="text-sm font-normal text-muted-foreground">
              honest inputs to honest scores
            </span>
          </h2>
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="18"
            height="18"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            class="text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-foreground transition-colors"
          >
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
            <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          A flight recorder sometimes logs an altitude that no glider can fly. GPS dropouts and
          multipath spikes cause these errors. Before the analysis, GlideComp repairs them: it
          compares the GPS altitude against the barometric channel, and uses physical
          plausibility limits when there is no barometer. The pilot's report card shows every
          repair. GlideComp never changes positions, times or the original file.
        </p>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-medium mt-3 text-foreground group-hover:underline">
          Read how data cleaning works
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="14"
            height="14"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
            <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
          </svg>
        </span>
      </a>

      {/* Track validity */}
      <a
        href="/scoring/track-validity"
        class="block mb-6 p-5 rounded-lg border border-border bg-card hover:border-primary/60 transition-colors group"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">
            Track validity checks
            <span class="text-sm font-normal text-muted-foreground">
              is this really your flight of this task?
            </span>
          </h2>
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="18"
            height="18"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            class="text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-foreground transition-colors"
          >
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
            <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          A pilot sometimes uploads the wrong file: a flight from another day, or from another
          site. GlideComp compares every tracklog against the task it was submitted to. It
          withholds a tracklog that cannot be that flight, instead of scoring it. Softer
          observations are only flagged, and never change a score. The scorekeeper can overrule
          every verdict.
        </p>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-medium mt-3 text-foreground group-hover:underline">
          Read how track validity works
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="14"
            height="14"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
            <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
          </svg>
        </span>
      </a>

      <div class="mt-10 pt-6 border-t border-border">
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">When the scoring changes</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          GlideComp corrects faults in its scoring, and moves it closer to the FAI
          specification, as it finds them. A change re-scores every competition, so your
          published points can move without the organiser touching anything. Every change is
          recorded, with what moved, who it affects and why.
          <a
            href="https://github.com/pokle/glidecomp/tree/master/web/engine/scoring-changes"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="underline hover:text-foreground"
          >
            Read the scoring changelog on GitHub</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
